    "result_text": "The build succeeds and the test passes. Let me verify the full picture is consistent by confirming the test count reflects everything green:\n\nThe suite is green \u2014 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` and `BUILD SUCCESS`. The audit line in the log confirms the new identity end-to-end: `customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity to `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, dropping sequence numbers, so every value derived from `customerCode` follows the new identity.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n- Replaced `nextCustomerCode(city, lastName)` (the old `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` per-city sequence) with `customerCode(postcode, normalizedTelephone, lastName)`, which builds `<REGION>-<HASH8>`:\n  - `regionFromPostcode(postcode)` \u2014 the region whose inclusive range contains the postcode (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099), else `UNKNOWN`.\n  - `sha256HexPrefix(normalizedTelephone + lastName, 8)` \u2014 first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256.\n- Updated the `addOwner` call site to pass the postcode, already-normalized telephone, and last name. The **create audit record** (`AUDIT.info(... customerCode ...)`) now emits the new identity with no code change since it reads `owner.getCustomerCode()`.\n- Removed a dangling `{@link #nextCustomerCode}` javadoc reference.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`**\n- `membershipNumber` (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`) and `checkDigit` (Luhn over the customerCode's digits) already read `customerCode`, so they automatically move to the new identity.\n- Rewrote `locality(owner)` to derive from the region-and-hash identity \u2014 the `REGION` prefix of `customerCode` \u2014 instead of independently recomputing region from postcode/city. Removed the now-unused `regionFromPostcode` helper and the `CITY_REGION` / `REGION_POSTCODES` constants.\n\nThis is a deliberate behaviour change (per the spec): identities and all derived values are now region-and-hash based, and locality falls out of the same `customerCode`.",
